# Files Docker leaves out of the image. One pattern per line; lines starting with # are notes.
# A pattern starting with **/ matches in this folder or any folder below it.

# Git's history and settings: the program doesn't need them, and they can hold old secrets.
.git

# Python and Node.js add-on folders, in any folder: big, and rebuilt inside the image if needed.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules

# Python's saved bytecode, in any folder.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Secret files such as API keys, in any folder: they must never go into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Key files and logs, in any folder: keys are secrets, and logs can hold private details.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.log

# Spreadsheet exports, in any folder: they can hold real listings, and this version reads none.
**/*.csv

# Claude Code and Superpowers settings, used while building, not while running.
.claude
.superpowers

# The task plans, the code review, the bug list and the feedback form: people read them,
# the program doesn't need them.
docs
REVIEW.md
BUGS.md
FEEDBACK.md

# The notes index (week 10): it holds the text of your notes, which can be private. To use it
# in a container, mount it at run time (see the README) instead of building it into the image.
**/notes-index.json

# Kept in the image on purpose: listings/ (two small sample listings). The program doesn't
# read them, but the live test (tests/test_live.py) does, so it can run inside the container.
# notes/ (the course's fictional investor notes) is kept too, so the index can be built and
# the notes live test can run inside the container.

# Claude Code MCP config: a path from one laptop, not needed in the image (week 11)
.mcp.json
